{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SpotLight3D","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A Spotlight is a type of "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Light3D","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" node that emits lights in a specific direction, in the shape of a cone. The light is attenuated through the distance. This attenuation can be configured by changing the energy, radius and attenuation parameters of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Light3D","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"style":"note","name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When using the Mobile rendering method, only 8 spot lights can be displayed on each mesh resource. Attempting to display more than 8 spot lights on a single mesh resource will result in spot lights flickering in and out as the camera moves. When using the Compatibility rendering method, only 8 spot lights can be displayed on each mesh resource by default, but this can be increased by adjusting "},{"code":"ProjectSettings\/rendering\/limits\/opengl\/maxLightsPerObject","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"type":"aside"},{"name":"Note","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When using the Mobile or Compatibility rendering methods, spot lights will only correctly affect meshes whose visibility AABB intersects with the light’s AABB. If using a shader to deform the mesh in a way that makes it go outside its AABB, ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GeometryInstance3D\/extraCullMargin"},{"type":"text","text":" must be increased on the mesh. Otherwise, the light may not be visible on the mesh."}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A spotlight, such as a reflector spotlight or a lantern."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/spotlight3d"]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/SpotLight3D\/spotAngle","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/SpotLight3D\/spotAngleAttenuation","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/SpotLight3D\/spotAttenuation","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/SpotLight3D\/spotRange"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/SpotLight3D\/godotClassName"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Properties","title":"Type Properties"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/SpotLight3D","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","title":"SpotLight3D","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"SpotLight3D","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SpotLight3D","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Class","modules":[{"name":"SwiftGodot"}],"externalID":"s:10SwiftGodot11SpotLight3DC","symbolKind":"class"},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Inherits From","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Light3D"],"type":"inheritsFrom"},{"type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/SQ","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/SH","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/s12IdentifiableP","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VariantConvertible"],"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relati